// The structured extractor (`Generator` in src/lean.rs) over `Id`: the
// functions the CFG extractor refuses that need no ambient monad (part 3a).
// It walks the source AST (ast.ves) and builds terms as word ranges
// (tm.ves) in Rust's evaluation order, so the first error is Rust's.
//
// What this part does not port yet sets `skip` instead of guessing:
// handlers and effect operations, effectful closures and calls, and types
// with effectful arrows (which need the `Id` monad in `ty`). The
// differential compares the other functions.

